<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistani road tankers resume strike.</title>
<headline>Pakistani road tankers resume strike.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistani road tanker owners have resumed a strike saying their demand for higher fees has not been implemented, a spokesman for the Oil Tankers Owners Association said on Monday.</p>
<p>The association had called off its 26-day old strike on Friday, but a dispute over the fee increase took the tankers, which carry vegetable oil and petroleum products, off the roads again on Sunday, the spokesman said.</p>
<p>The strike cut oil supplies to mills, resulting in lower production of processed edible oils, driving up local prices.</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
